docs/llm-wiki/log.md merge=union
docs/llm-wiki/index.md merge=union

# Append-only for the same reason log.md is, and left out of this list until five merge
# conflicts in one day said so (#252). Every branch is required to update it, so two open
# branches always collide at the tail, and the resolution was "keep both" every single time.
# `union` keeps both with no marker — which is wrong for a file that gets edited in place and
# right for one that only ever grows a dated section at the end.
.harness/state/progress.md merge=union

# Measured protocol captures are byte-exact evidence, not source text. Git's line-ending
# translation would let the checkout platform decide what our evidence says — on Windows
# (core.autocrlf=true by default, including CI runners) the raw newlines inside a captured
# `value` attribute become CRLF and the capture no longer matches what Programmers served.
src/test/resources/fixtures/** -text

